  <h1>The Rain That Was Killing Lakes: How Cap-and-Trade Fixed Acid Rain</h1>
  <p class="dek">In the 1970s, rain was killing lakes across the United States. Scientists spent 18 years trying to prove it. The fix came from an unlikely source: a market mechanism that worked better than anyone predicted.</p>
